schema: '0.4'
id: vis_js-02-dense-stress-layout
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: vis_js
category: network-and-graph-visualization
variant: dense-graph-stress-layout
prompt:
  context:
  - references/fim/overview/network-3d-graphics/vis_js.md
  - references/fim/solution/vis_js.md
  text: 'Build a vis-network dense-graph stress demo for a 2500-node service graph.

    Use clustering, hidden low-priority edges, stabilization iterations, a physics

    solver such as forceAtlas2Based or barnesHut, and a handler that disables

    physics after stabilizationIterationsDone. Include controls to cluster by hub

    size, open clusters on double click, hide labels while zoomed out, and switch

    to precomputed x/y positions with physics false when counts exceed the live

    simulation threshold. Report node count, edge count, cluster count, layout

    duration, and stabilization progress.

    '
  system: You generate artifacts for vis_js. Output only the requested artifact content. No markdown fences, no explanations.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 6144
    temperature: 0.3
output:
  formats:
  - format: html
  - format: json
  renderer: vis-network-canvas
  expected_artifact: Dense vis-network stress page with clustering and metrics.
  text_format: vis_js
  artifact_kind: Dense vis-network stress page with clustering and metrics.
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - Uses vis-network clustering and stabilization controls.
  - Disables physics after stabilization for performance.
  - Includes precomputed-position fallback for excessive graph size.
  - Reports layout and clustering metrics.
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    description: YAML parses and declares visualization plus metrics outputs.
    criteria: YAML parses and declares visualization plus metrics outputs.
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    description: Covers dense graph physics, clustering, stabilization, fallback, and telemetry.
    criteria: Covers dense graph physics, clustering, stabilization, fallback, and telemetry.
  - name: Visual/structural quality
    weight: 25
    description: Dense graph remains navigable through clustering and label controls.
    criteria: Dense graph remains navigable through clustering and label controls.
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    description: Avoids continuous physics cost and warns beyond vis-network limits.
    criteria: Avoids continuous physics cost and warns beyond vis-network limits.
  pass_conditions:
  - The prompt respects vis-network's mid-size graph ceiling.
  - Dense stress metrics and stabilization progress are included.
  - Cluster open and fallback behavior are specified.
tags:
- fim
- vis-js
- vis-network
- dense-graph
- stress-layout
- clustering
- stabilization
